# MVVM Presentation

Source of truth: `iOSApp/AGENT.md` §3, §5, §9, §10.

## Views

Views only render state and forward actions to the ViewModel.

```swift
// ✅
struct ChatView: View {
    @StateObject private var viewModel: ChatViewModel

    init(viewModel: ChatViewModel) {
        _viewModel = StateObject(wrappedValue: viewModel)
    }

    var body: some View {
        ScrollView { /* read viewModel.* */ }
            .task { await viewModel.loadSession() }
    }
}

// ❌ Never call LLM/DB/API from body; no business if/else beyond UI branching
// ❌ Never .onAppear { Task { await viewModel.load… } } — use .task / .task(id:)
```

- **Async tied to the view:** `.task { }` or `.task(id:) { }` — never `Task` inside `.onAppear` (see `ios-swift-conventions.mdc`)
- Local UI only: `@State`, `@FocusState`
- Screen ViewModel: **`@StateObject`** — single source of truth ([Apple](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/stateobject)); DI via `_viewModel = StateObject(wrappedValue:)`
- Child that only observes a parent-owned object: `@ObservedObject` / `@EnvironmentObject`
- App-wide: `@EnvironmentObject` (`AppRouter`, `AppContainer`)
- Different `sessionId` / identity → `.id(...)` so `@StateObject` reinits

## ViewModels

```swift
@MainActor
final class ChatViewModel: ObservableObject {
    @Published private(set) var messages: [MessageDisplayModel] = []
    @Published var isLoading = false
    @Published var errorMessage: String?

    private let saveMemoryUseCase: SaveMemoryUseCaseProtocol
    private let router: AppRouter

    init(saveMemoryUseCase: SaveMemoryUseCaseProtocol, router: AppRouter) {
        self.saveMemoryUseCase = saveMemoryUseCase
        self.router = router
    }

    func sendMessage() async {
        isLoading = true
        defer { isLoading = false }
        // call use cases only — never DatabaseManager / LLMClient directly
    }
}
```

- Import `Foundation` + `Combine` only — never `SwiftUI`
- Dependencies only via `init` — never `SomeThing()` inside the VM
- Convert domain → display models in the ViewModel (formatted strings, icons, theme colors)
- Navigate with `router.navigate(to:)` — not `NavigationLink` destinations in list rows

## UI composition

Feature screens **compose** `Core/Theme/Components` (e.g. one `ChatBubble` for user + assistant via `isUser`). Do not restyle with raw colors in Features. See `ios-ui-components.mdc` and `docs/design/theme-guide.md`.
